d Table by Priority ascending independently. Switched back to Cards: it retained its own earlier \\\"Priority descending\\\" sort, unaffected by Table's sort - confirming independent, auto-saved per-view sort state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature implemented\", \"actual\": \"No UI control, button, icon, or menu for defining filter criteria exists anywhere in the app. Only a sort menu and a search box are present.\", \"evidence\": \"Full-page DOM search (case-insensitive) for the string \\\"filter\\\" and for a \\\"lucide-filter\\\" icon class returned zero matches; header toolbar only contains Search box, Sort button, Table/Cards toggle, and Add Entry button.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With no sort active, used drag-handle keyboard interaction (Space to pick up, Arrow to move, Space to drop) to manually reorder entries in Table view (Design moved from position 1 to 3) and separately in Cards view (Design moved from position 1 to 5). After switching views, Table retained order [Review, Update, Design, Prepare, Team sync, Test Alpha] while Cards retained a different order [Review, Update, Prepare, Team sync, Design, Test Alpha] - confirming independent manual order per view.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No import feature implemented\", \"actual\": \"No import button, file input, or import UI exists anywhere in the app despite the Fields dialog note stating \\\"Configure fields before importing data.\\\"\", \"evidence\": \"Full-page DOM search for \\\"import\\\" (case-insensitive) found only the single note-text occurrence in the Fields dialog; no input[type=file] elements exist in the document.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Priority field is a native input[type=number]. Attempting to type non-numeric text \\\"abc\\\" into it was rejected outright (Playwright error: \\\"Cannot type text into input[type=number]\\\"). Entering valid number 42 was accepted and saved correctly, displayed as \\\"42\\\" in both views.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Due Date field is a native input[type=date]. Setting an invalid date value \\\"2026-13-45\\\" resulted in the field value becoming empty (browser-level rejection). Setting a valid date \\\"2026-09-10\\\" was accepted and saved correctly, displayed as \\\"Sep 10, 2026\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sorting Table/Cards by Priority ascending and descending preserved entry count at 6 throughout, and all field values (Task Name, Priority, Due Date, Completed, Notes) for every entry remained unchanged - only row/card order changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature implemented\", \"actual\": \"Filtering criteria cannot be defined, applied, or cleared since no filter UI exists in the app.\", \"evidence\": \"Same as FT-6: full-page DOM search found no filter-related controls anywhere.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inconsistent empty-value representation\", \"actual\": \"Empty values are not given a consistent, clear representation. Entries whose Notes field was never set (e.g. pre-existing entries after the field was added later) show a \\\"—\\\" placeholder in both Table and Cards views. However, an entry created via the Add Entry form with the Notes field left blank (\\\"Number Test Entry\\\") shows a completely blank cell/attribute value with no placeholder at all, in both views.\", \"evidence\": \"DOM check: existing rows' Notes <td> contains \\\"—\\\"; \\\"Number Test Entry\\\" row's Notes <td> is empty string. Same blank (no dash) confirmed in Cards view for that entry's Notes attribute.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Field type selector in Configure Fields dialog clearly lists labeled options: Text, Number, Date, Checkbox (each with icon). Add Entry form renders type-appropriate controls: text textbox for Text field, native number spinbutton for Number field, native date input for Date field, and a checkbox with Yes/No label for Checkbox field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In Add Entry form, checkbox toggles between \\\"Completed No\\\" and \\\"Completed Yes\\\" labeled states. In Table view, checked entries render a green \\\"check\\\" icon (text-success class) while unchecked render a muted \\\"x\\\" icon. In Cards view, checked/unchecked entries show explicit \\\"Yes\\\"/\\\"No\\\" text alongside icons.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Search matches only raw internal values, not displayed formatted values\", \"actual\": \"Searching for the displayed date format \\\"Jan 15\\\" returned 0 results even though an entry's Due Date is displayed as \\\"Jan 15, 2026\\\". Searching for the raw ISO value \\\"2026-01-15\\\" did return that entry (1 match). Searching for the displayed checkbox state \\\"Yes\\\" (shown in Cards view for Completed=true entries) returned 0 results.\", \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"Jan 15\\\" -> \\\"0 entries matching\\\". Search \\\"2026-01-15\\\" -> \\\"1 entry matching\\\" (Design new landing page). Search \\\"Yes\\\" -> \\\"0 entries matching\\\" despite multiple entries showing Completed: Yes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"review\\\" (lowercase) into search box matched \\\"Review marketing materials\\\" (case-insensitive), updated the count label to '1 entry matching \\\"review\\\"', and clearing the search box restored all 6 entries with the count returning to \\\"6 entries\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selecting \\\"Priority\\\" from the Sort menu immediately reordered visible entries ascending; the Sort button label changed to \\\"Priority\\\" (active) and the footer showed \\\"Sorted by Priority (ascending)\\\". Re-selecting toggled to \\\"Sorted by Priority (descending)\\\" with entries re-ordered accordingly. App remained fully interactive afterward (menu, view toggle, search all functioned normally).\"}]}"
